  "notes": "Source spells names in ALL CAPS in ASCII; converted to Title Case here (first letter upper, rest lower; 'MARIA VITTORIA' -> 'Maria Vittoria'). The source has no accented letters: it writes Nicolo and Niccolo with a trailing apostrophe in place of the accent (\"NICOLO'\", \"NICCOLO'\"), kept as \"Nicolo'\" and \"Niccolo'\"; plain 'Nicolo' (rank 86 male) is a separate source row, so Nicolo, Nicolo' and Niccolo' are variants of one name (Nicolo with grave accent) that a reviewer may want to merge. Ranks are the source's order (descending count); there are ties in count (1 male, 3 female) where the source's order was kept. Source stores one row per spelling, so spelling variants (e.g. Sophia/Sofia, Cristian/Christian, Nicolas/Nicholas) are counted separately; compound names are one entry. Istat applies no corrections for typos or name/sex mismatches (page footnote). The page UI hides counts under 5; none occur in the top 100. Implied 2024 totals from the source's percent column: about 189,358 male and 179,169 female births. Raw response saved in the scratchpad as list2024_100.json. Data is national (Italy), not a city or region.",
  "source_id": "src_name_frequency_it_it_istat"
}
